(Linux Fundamentals) Tj T*
(Course summary | Instructor: Beau Carnes) Tj T*
T*
(A short summary of the course: what Linux is, how to move around the command line, and how files,) Tj T*
(editors and permissions work.) Tj T*
T*
(Week 1-2) Tj T*
(What is Linux) Tj T*
(Linux is an open-source kernel created by Linus Torvalds in 1991. Together with GNU tools it forms a) Tj T*
(full operating system used on servers, phones \(Android\), embedded devices and supercomputers.) Tj T*
T*
(Distributions and Installation) Tj T*
(A distribution bundles the kernel with software and a package manager. Popular ones are Ubuntu,) Tj T*
(Debian, Fedora and Arch. You usually install from a bootable USB image.) Tj T*
T*
(The Graphical Interface) Tj T*
(Desktop environments such as GNOME, KDE Plasma and Xfce provide windows, menus and file) Tj T*
(managers. They are optional: servers usually run without any graphical interface.) Tj T*
T*
(The Linux Philosophy) Tj T*
(Programs should do one thing well. Everything is treated as a file, text is the common interface, and) Tj T*
(small programs are combined with pipes \(|\).) Tj T*
T*
(Week 3-4) Tj T*
(Basic Commands) Tj T*
(Use pwd to print the current directory, ls to list files, cd to move between directories and man to read) Tj T*
(a command's manual. Options such as ls -l change the output.) Tj T*
T*
(Working with Files) Tj T*
(Create with touch and mkdir, copy with cp, move or rename with mv, delete with rm. rm -r) Tj T*
(removes directories and cannot be undone. Read files with cat or less.) Tj T*
T*
(Text Editors) Tj T*
(nano is simple and shows its shortcuts on screen. vim is modal: press i to insert text, Esc to return) Tj T*
(to normal mode, and :wq to save and quit \(:q! quits without saving\).) Tj T*
T*
(Users and Permissions) Tj T*
(Every file has an owner, a group and permissions for read, write and execute. chmod 755 file) Tj T*
(gives the owner full access and others read and execute. sudo runs a command as the superuser.) Tj T*
T*
(Quick reference) Tj T*
(pwd                                   Print the working directory) Tj T*
(ls -la                                List all files with details) Tj T*
(cd ..                                 Go up one directory) Tj T*
(chmod +x file                         Make a file executable) Tj T*
ET
